{
 "method": "Exact Clopper-Pearson 95% intervals (alpha=0.05) via scipy.stats.beta: lower=beta.ppf(a/2,k,n-k+1) (0 if k=0), upper=beta.ppf(1-a/2,k+1,n-k) (1 if k=n). Two views per threshold factor. (1) per_level_pooled: at each discrete factor level the worst-case decoder = lowest pooled decode rate; CP on pooled k of n (n = cells_at_level x captures_per_cell). (2) boundary_cell: the single design cell (one cid) at the factor level nearest the reported P95 threshold, its own worst-case decoder's k of N, CP on that. Occlusion = results.parquet exp=G1 & ppm>=4 per EC (N=16 per cell, 3 cells/level -> pooled n=48). Contrast = results.parquet exp=G2 & ~inverted & ppm>=4 (N=16 per cell, 12 cells/level -> pooled n=192). PPM cliff = results_cliff.parquet payload=med per EC (N=40 per cell, 1 cell/level -> pooled n=40; here the boundary cell N=40, not 16). Reported thresholds and subsets match headline.py.",
